  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(36, 24, 65)\n\n(40, 54, 19)\n\n**Logic:** Third no. = [(First no. ÷ 4)² - (Second no. ÷ 6)²]\n\n**(36, 24, 65) →**\n\n⇒ [(36 ÷ 4)2 - (24 ÷ 6)2]\n\n⇒ [(9)² - (4)²]\n\n⇒ (81 - 16) = 65\n\n**(40, 54, 19) →**\n\n⇒ [(40 ÷ 4)2 - (54 ÷ 6)2]\n\n⇒ [(10)2 - (9)2]\n\n⇒ (100 - 81) = 19\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. **(10, 21, 321)\n\n⇒ [(10 ÷ 4)2 - (21 ÷ 6)2]\n\n⇒ [(2.5)2 - (3.5)2]\n\n⇒ (6.25 - 12.25) = (-6)\n\n**2. (20, 18, 16)**\n\n⇒ [(20 ÷ 4)2 - (18 ÷ 6)2]\n\n⇒ [(5)2 - (3)2]\n\n⇒ (25 - 9) =** 16**\n\n**3.** (13, 8, 98)\n\n⇒ [(13 ÷ 4)2 - (8 ÷ 6)2]\n\n⇒ [(3.25)2 - (1.33)2]\n\n⇒ (10.56 - 1.77) = 8.78\n\n**4.** (30, 14, 56)\n\n⇒ [(30 ÷ 4)2 - (14 ÷ 6)2]\n\n⇒ [(7.5)2 - (2.33)2]\n\n⇒ (56.25 - 5.44) = 50.81\n\nHere,** (20, 18, 16) **shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (2)\".",
